=== Complete Solutions

#sol-item(1, "B", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[A pathogen is an organism or infectious agent capable of causing disease. A pathogen and the symptoms it produces are not the same thing.]

#sol-item(2, "D", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[Some infections do not produce noticeable symptoms. Absence of visible symptoms does not establish that infection is absent.]

#sol-item(3, "A", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[Communicable diseases can spread directly or indirectly under suitable conditions. Spread depends on the infectious agent, route and circumstances.]

#sol-item(4, "D", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[Several classes of infectious agents can cause disease. Not every organism in these groups causes disease.]

#sol-item(5, "D", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[A route describes how an infectious agent can reach a host. A route identifies a possible pathway, not a certain outcome.]

#sol-item(6, "A", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[Transmission depends on the agent and circumstances.]

#sol-item(7, "A", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[Some respiratory infections spread through infectious particles in air.]

#sol-item(8, "C", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[Contaminated food and water can transmit some diarrhoeal pathogens.]

#sol-item(9, "D", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[A vector is an organism that can transmit an agent.]

#sol-item(10, "C", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[Prevention should address the actual pathogen and pathway.]

#sol-item(11, "C", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[Plasmodium parasites cause malaria.]

#sol-item(12, "D", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[Infected female Anopheles mosquitoes are common malaria vectors.]

#sol-item(13, "B", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[Fever is not specific to malaria and needs appropriate evaluation.]

#sol-item(14, "A", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[Appropriate assessment and testing help guide diagnosis and treatment.]

#sol-item(15, "C", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[Confusion or breathing difficulty can signal severe illness and needs urgent help.]

#sol-item(16, "A", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[Treated nets are an important part of malaria prevention but do not eliminate all risk.]

#sol-item(17, "B", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[Eligibility and suitability depend on current programmes and individual circumstances.]

#sol-item(18, "D", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[Safe water and sanitation interrupt important pathways for some infections.]

#sol-item(19, "C", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[Fluid loss from diarrhoea can cause dehydration.]

#sol-item(20, "B", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[Severe symptoms and inability to drink require timely assessment.]

#sol-item(21, "D", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[TB is caused by bacteria, commonly affecting the lungs.]

#sol-item(22, "B", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[Infectious pulmonary TB can spread through airborne particles.]

#sol-item(23, "C", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[A persistent cough has several possible causes and needs assessment.]

#sol-item(24, "B", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[Ventilation can reduce exposure to some airborne pathogens in suitable settings.]

#sol-item(25, "B", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[HIV is a virus that affects the immune system.]

#sol-item(26, "C", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[Certain blood and other body-fluid exposures can transmit HIV; casual contact does not.]

#sol-item(27, "A", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[WHO states that HIV is not spread by ordinary social contact such as hugging or sharing food.]

#sol-item(28, "C", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[Contaminated needles can transmit infections through blood exposure.]

#sol-item(29, "B", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[Parent-to-baby transmission can occur during pregnancy, birth or breastfeeding; care can reduce risk.]

#sol-item(30, "C", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[ART treats HIV and can suppress viral load, but does not cure HIV.]

#sol-item(31, "B", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[WHO states that people with sustained undetectable viral load do not sexually transmit HIV.]

#sol-item(32, "D", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[Condoms reduce risk when used correctly and consistently, but do not remove every risk.]

#sol-item(33, "A", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[Stigma can discourage testing, support and treatment.]

#sol-item(34, "B", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[Vaccines target particular agents and are one part of prevention.]

#sol-item(35, "A", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[Schedules vary by vaccine, programme and circumstances.]

#sol-item(36, "A", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[Antibiotics work against susceptible bacteria, not viral infections.]

#sol-item(37, "A", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[Testing is one part of diagnosis and care.]

#sol-item(38, "C", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[A net targets mosquito exposure, not contamination in drinking water.]

#sol-item(39, "D", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[Respectful, evidence-based communication avoids stigma and misinformation.]

#sol-item(40, "D", dense: true, pad: 3pt)[Different routes require appropriate interventions, and access to care matters.]
